    "## 2. Descriptive, Predictive, Prescriptive\n",
    "\n",
    "Analytics work usually flows through three stages. The cricket analogy makes them\n",
    "click instantly:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Stage | Question | Cricket example |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| **Descriptive** | What happened? It locates and isolates the problem. | How many centuries has the batsman scored? (look it up) |\n",
    "| **Predictive** | What *will* happen, or what happens if I change something? | How many centuries will he score in the World Cup? |\n",
    "| **Prescriptive** | What should I *do* to change the outcome? | How do we get him to score *more* centuries? |\n",
    "\n",
    "A doctor does all three: *describe* your symptoms, *predict* you are becoming\n",
    "pre-diabetic, then *prescribe* an action - under constraints (first, do no harm).\n",
    "A business does the same: sell more watches, but stay profitable, keep employees,\n",
    "repay loans. Prescription is a constrained optimization problem.\n",
    "\n",
    "**This notebook focuses mostly on the descriptive foundation**, because everything\n",
    "predictive and prescriptive is built on top of it."
   ]
  },
