    "## 3. A dataset to think with: CardioGoodFitness\n",
    "\n",
    "The market-research team of a fitness company wants the **profile of the typical\n",
    "customer** for each treadmill product. They collect data on people who bought a\n",
    "treadmill in the last three months.\n",
    "\n",
    "We generate a synthetic version of the well-known *CardioGoodFitness* dataset so\n",
    "every cell here runs with no external file. The columns mirror the real study:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `Product` - model bought (TM195, TM498, TM798)\n",
    "- `Gender`, `Age`, `Education` (years),\n",
    "- `MaritalStatus`\n",
    "- `Income` - annual household income\n",
    "- `Usage` - times per week the customer plans to use it\n",
    "- `Fitness` - self-rated 1 (poor) to 5 (excellent)\n",
    "- `Miles` - expected miles walked/run per week\n",
    "\n",
    "Notice that some of these are **measured facts** (age, income) and some are\n",
    "**opinion masquerading as data** (planned usage, self-rated fitness). It's still\n",
    "data - it came from somewhere."
   ]
