    "## 7b. Where quartiles, IQR & percentiles are really used\n",
    "\n",
    "Now the important part: **why are you learning this, and where does it show up in a real job?**\n",
    "\n",
    "Quartiles (Q1, Q2, Q3), the IQR, and percentiles are not just textbook terms - they are the everyday tools a data scientist uses to **clean data, rank things, and split customers into groups**. Below are the three most common real-life jobs they do, each with runnable code on our treadmill data.\n",
    "\n",
    "Quick reminder of the four quarters:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "|  Q1   |   Q2    |   Q3   |   Q4  |\n",
    " lowest   second    third   highest\n",
    "  25%      25%       25%      25%\n",
    "        (Q2 = median = the middle)\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Q1** = 25th percentile (bottom quarter ends here)\n",
    "- **Q2** = 50th percentile = the **median** (the middle)\n",
    "- **Q3** = 75th percentile (top quarter starts here)\n",
    "- **IQR** = Q3 - Q1 = the span of the middle 50%"
   ]
